translation:
Now, the characteristics of a practitioner of the highest and most intense degree:
One endowed with great valor and enthusiasm, pleasing, and also courageous;
Learned in scriptures and diligent in practice, free from delusion, and undisturbed;
Possessing fresh youth, moderate in diet, and one who has conquered the senses;
And fearless, pure, skillful, generous, a refuge for all people;
Competent, steady, intelligent, abiding by his own will, patient;
Of good character, practicing righteousness, of hidden endeavors, and pleasant-spoken;
Endowed with faith in scriptures, worshipper of deities and guru;
And unattached to the company of people, free from great diseases;
And observing supreme vows, a practitioner of all Yoga.
For such a one, success (siddhi) comes within three years; there is no doubt about this.
He is competent for all forms of Yoga; no deliberation is required here.

